DeepSeek V4 Flash is a massive 284 billion parameter Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) AI model
. In this video, we set up and run it fully locally on a single consumer APU—the AMD Ryzen AI Max+ 395 featuring the Radeon 8060S GPU and 125GB of unified memory
. Using a cutting-edge, custom C++ inference engine called "loose-box," we hit a blazing-fast local inference speed of 32 tokens per second
!
"loose-box" is a custom-compiled C++ server binary that bypasses Python, vLLM, or llama.cpp entirely, talking directly to the AMD GPU over ROCm HIP
.
To break past the standard 22–25 tokens per second autoregressive baseline, we implement Speculative Decoding via the "DSpark" draft model with a Q=4 verification cap
. This allows a tiny, fast draft model to guess upcoming tokens while the massive 284B target model verifies them in a single, fused GPU forward pass
. The result is a massive 26% performance gain entirely on consumer AMD hardware
. We also dive into how DeepSeek V4 Flash uses built-in Multi-Token Prediction (MTP) heads to predict additional tokens per pass without requiring extra memory or downloading a second model
.
Watch as we walk through the custom C++ server build, configure CPU performance modes, lock the GPU clock speeds, and stream coherent local responses in real-time over raw HTTP
.

